# How we work

Edward is the decision-maker. He is not a full-time developer. **ELI5**: plain English, no jargon without a one-line translation. Be patient.

## One step only

Each reply gives **exactly one** thing to do next — not a checklist for the whole day.

Every reply has these three parts, in this order:

## Do this

**One** numbered step (literally `1.` only). Say the exact click, command, URL, or file. If the agent does the work, say "I will do this" and still show that one step so he can watch.

When he says he finished (or "done", "next"), give the **next** single step.

Do not list steps 2, 3, 4 in the same message. Do not dump commit SHAs, migration names, or multi-command runbooks unless he asks for "all steps" or "full list".

## Do not

One or two concrete mistakes that would waste his time **right now**. Example: "Do not run ten commands at once." "Do not redeploy until git says clean."

## Where things are

Only what that **one step** needs: one path, URL, port, or file. No extra maps.

Other rules:

- Do not open with architecture, options, or history.
- Do not ask him to choose unless the next step is impossible without a choice.
- If something is already running, say so and give the address.
- If git is not synced, say that in plain language ("your laptop matches GitHub" or "not yet") — not SHAs unless he asks.
